{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.harmonic_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.harmonic_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L241-L250","doc":"`HM = 2/([2]_q·[2]_{q²})`, and with `arithmetic_pinned` and `GM = 1/[2]_q`\nthis completes `AM·HM = GM²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.arithmetic_pinned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.arithmetic_pinned","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L233-L239","doc":"`AM = [2]_{q²}/(2[2]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_harmonic_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_harmonic_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L211-L217","doc":"**So the harmonic mean gives the SEMF sign**, for any positive bonds. It is\nrecorded as a TARGET a derivation may be checked against — never as a criterion\nto search on, and nothing here adopts it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_harmonic_eq_neg_delta_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_harmonic_eq_neg_delta_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L195-L209","doc":"**The harmonic mean is the arithmetic mean's exact mirror.** `δ` flips sign\nand keeps its magnitude, so the wrong-signed `-0.0216177…` at `p = 1` is\n`+0.0216177…` at `p = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.harmonic_mul_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.harmonic_mul_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L190-L193","doc":"`HM · AM = a·b`, the `p = ±1` case of `M_p · M_{-p} = ab`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_miss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_miss","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L165-L174","doc":"**The miss against the crossing, split.** The deformation term\n`(q²-1)/(2(q²+1))` and the flavour term `δ/4` are the only two contributions,\nand at `q₀` the first is 151× the second — so the flavour split, the one derived\ningredient in `w`, is irrelevant to the sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_of_convention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_of_convention","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L159-L163","doc":"**The convex weight is forced by the averaging convention.** Given the three\ninterface factors, `w = 1/2 + δ/4` is an identity, not a choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.am_sub_gm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.am_sub_gm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L132-L142","doc":"**The AM–GM gap IS the Hecke parameter, squared.**\n`(b_pp+b_nn)/2 - 1/[2]_q = h²/(2[2]_q)` with `h = q - 1/q`, because\n`[2]_q² - 4 = h²`. The size of the wrong-signed term is not incidental to the\ndeformation — it is the deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.crossing_lt_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.crossing_lt_half","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**No `q > 1` rescues an equal-weight construction.** The crossing `1/(q²+1)`\nis `1/2` only at `q = 1` and strictly below it thereafter, while the corpus holds\nthe weight at `1/2 + δ_flavour/4`. This is `qou-q7ga`'s \"the q-deformation is\nnet-negative on binding\", with a mechanism: the deformation moves the threshold\ndown, the construction does not follow it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.convex_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.convex_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The convex combination is strictly increasing in the weight when the p–p\nbond is the larger. So a weight ABOVE the crossing puts `b_pn` above the\ngeometric mean, which by `delta_nonpos_iff` is the wrong side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.crossing_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.crossing_weight","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L101-L113","doc":"**The crossing weight, in the pinned case.** With `b_pp = q²/[2]_q` and\n`b_nn = q⁻²/[2]_q` the geometric mean is `1/[2]_q`, and the convex weight that\nlands exactly on it is `w = 1/(q²+1)`. Stated as the identity rather than as an\ninequality, because the identity is what a reader checks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_midpoint_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_midpoint_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L94-L99","doc":"**An equal-weight p–n bond is always wrong-signed.** Nothing about `q`, the\ngraph or the scale enters: the midpoint of two positives is never below their\ngeometric mean, so `δ ≤ 0` however the letters come out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.sqrt_mul_le_midpoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.sqrt_mul_le_midpoint","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**AM–GM in the two-variable form the bond letters need.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_nonpos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta_nonpos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L74-L85","doc":"**The sign question is the AM-vs-GM question.** `δ ≤ 0` — the wrong sign —\nexactly when `b_pn` is at least the geometric mean of the like-species bonds.\nEverything else in this file is about which side of that mean the construction\nputs `b_pn` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.SymmetrySignAmGm.delta","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/SymmetrySignAmGm.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The p–n slope: how the bond sum changes when one like-species pair of bonds\nis traded for a p–n bond, in the corpus's `L = -log b` letters. Positive means\nmixing binds more — the SEMF sign. ","signatureChunk":0}]}